# Line endings — deliberately NARROW. Read the scope note before widening this.
#
# This repo is Syncthing-mirrored across a Mac, a Windows PC and the box. With no
# .gitattributes and core.autocrlf unset, source files flip CRLF <-> LF on their
# own: src/lib/mapping/map-ingredient-with-fallback.ts was 6,531 CRLF lines at
# abbe55a and 0 from c16a24e onward, with no commit intending the change.
#
# That flip tripped the winner-diff drift guard on selection code that had not
# changed — the guard reported DRIFT against a caller block byte-identical to the
# shape it transcribes. The guard now normalizes line endings before hashing, which
# is the real fix; this file stops the churn reaching the guard's inputs at all.
#
# SCOPE: pinned to the three files the drift guard reads (stage 1a moved the
# COPIED_HELPERS bodies into serving/hydration-lane.ts). All are already LF in the
# index, so this is a zero-diff change — verify with `git add --renormalize .` on a
# clean tree, which must report nothing.
#
# A repo-wide `*.ts text eol=lf` would renormalize 76 of 646 tracked TypeScript
# files (measured 2026-08-03) and, because Syncthing carries working-tree files,
# push that rewrite to all three machines. That may well be worth doing — but as its
# own reviewed commit, not as a side effect of fixing an eval harness.
src/lib/mapping/map-ingredient-with-fallback.ts text eol=lf
scripts/eval/winner-diff.ts text eol=lf
src/lib/mapping/serving/hydration-lane.ts text eol=lf
